From: djnice <djnice77@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:38:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dvfel: compose the hardware decoded EL

With the dvfel module that takes a decoded EL (its el_wait_ms parameter),
a FEL title keeps its EL in the stream and the decoder is opened for Dolby
Vision dual layer: the S5 decodes both layers, dvfel hands the decoded EL
picture of each frame to the compositor with the BL, and the EL no longer
costs CPU (Kodi 5-9 % instead of all cores on heavy remuxes). The Dolby
Vision core still gets the converted no-op RPU.

- the EL is kept from the first access unit (its parameter sets)
- felgpu takes the EL as a texture (unpack pass) instead of a CPU frame
- the RPU is found by the frame's pts; an EL coded in another picture order
  than the BL (dvfel reports different access units for the pair, paired by
  display order) takes the RPU of its own access unit, like the software
  EL decoder does
- /storage/dvfel_sw_el keeps the software EL decoder, for comparisons

- a MEL title (or one without the composition) gets its first access unit
  without the EL NAL units kept for the hardware decoder, else the decoder
  switched to dual layer and Dolby Vision never engaged (HDR10)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
